# Family A7: fan-out admission policy (internal/engine). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/engine
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/FanOut
REF=atomic
AUTO_KEY=fanout
KIND_DIM=policy
KINDS_TEST=TestFanoutKindsList
AUTO_FILE=./internal/engine/auto_fanout.go
AUTO_PREFIX=Fanout
ADR=14
TITLE="Fan-out admission policy (A7)"
# The §9 criterion is correctness first, then overhead: Atomic stays the
# default unless another policy is within 5 %. The slow=1 arm is what the
# policies exist for and is reported alongside the throughput.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="correctness first; overhead <= 5% -> Atomic default, others opt-in"
# MATRIX=default: the overhead the criterion bounds is read against the
# reference policy at every fan-out width the default grid produces, and the
# partial-delivery accounting the row asks for is read at slow=1, which it also
# produces. `full`'s 256-subscription width reads nothing.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="1 16 slow=0 slow=1"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op partial/op refused/op"
SHARES_ROOT="A2"
